{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-mixed-demo-review", "file": "references/cellwise-mask-and-generator-validation.md", "content": "# Cellwise mask validation across heterogeneous demos

When an ARC task has a distinctive colored seed in noisy grids, do not equate resemblance with the rule. Track the seed shape, eligible target values, and spatial generator as independent hypotheses. For every demo, enumerate the full input/output difference mask and preserve negative evidence: unchanged lookalikes, untouched target-valued cells, and the original seed.

Before another demo or a submission, replay the proposed generator against every pair, especially when seed shape, palette, or dimensions vary. A literal translated-template matcher that looks plausible on one example but fails the varied demos is falsified; do not patch it by shifting a few cells. Request additional examples only for explicit remaining alternatives and a specific discriminating observation.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-seq0/frozen/seen/play/users/u026/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-mixed-demo-review/references/cellwise-mask-and-generator-validation.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-error-recovery", "file": "references/multi-rejection-demo-discipline.md", "content": "# Multi-rejection discipline for demo-driven ARC

In a task with one or more incorrect submissions, an incorrect result falsifies the whole proposed generator. Do not resubmit a near-identical grid or make an evidence-free palette/coordinate tweak. Rebuild a ledger from every input-output pair, including unchanged cells, and separately test scope, geometry, mapping, and palette.

When multiple candidate grids have failed and the remaining evidence does not determine the test output, stop guessing. State internally at least two concrete hypotheses and the specific observation that distinguishes them. Request one demo only if it can supply that observation, then integrate it before the next action; never treat receiving a demo as an automatic reason for another request. Submit only when one candidate explains every pair and unambiguously yields the test grid. Keep each turn to one action-only JSON object.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-seq0/frozen/seen/play/users/u026/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-error-recovery/references/multi-rejection-demo-discipline.md"}

